OL,1,D]S(|$|h4|$ |,h<h<h<`<th4| h<h4| |$|,   
OL,2,D]S  k51 pjwjwj7j7h7} j7j501s   
OL,3,T///,/,-.,./,,-,-,-.-.,-.,/-.-.,.,.,,///
OL,4,CCOP31 climate talks end with no deal   
OL,5,Cafter fossil fuels row derails hopes   
OL,6,Cof agreement                           
OL,7,FThe talks have been the longest-       
OL,8,Frunning in the summit's history, with  
OL,9,Fnegotiations breaking down two days    
OL,10,Fafter they had been due to end -       
OL,11,Fhere's a timeline of how we got here.  
OL,13,FAustralian minister Chris Bowen,       
OL,14,FCOP31's president of negotiations,     
OL,15,Fsays the summit faced the "most        
OL,16,Fcomplicated and fraught geopolitical   
OL,17,Fenvironment in living memory".         
OL,19,FUK Energy Secretary Miatta Fahnbulleh  
OL,20,Fsays it is "disappointing" that the    
OL,21,Ftalks did not manage to "build         
OL,22,Fconsensus" between parties.       G2/3 
